{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>and to rule</b> — the day of the Torah is from the time the sun emerges until it sets, and the night from the time the stars are seen. And those who say 'on the basis of three witnesses' were correct. Know that the time when the sun darkens is evening until the third of an hour when light like that appears in the clouds, and likewise the morning light is before the sun's rising. And with the emergence of the sun's light by day and the moon's light by night, they distinguish between the light and the darkness."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase 'and they were correct who said on the basis of three witnesses' is opaque; rendered hyper-literally without resolving its referent."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:17.255724916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}